PIXEL REALM — a 16-bit pocket RPG
=================================

A complete browser-based, 16-bit pixel-art RPG. No build step, no
dependencies — every sprite is procedurally rendered onto an HTML5
canvas at runtime from compact text patterns.

Just open `index.html` (or serve the folder with any static server)
and play.

Features
--------
- Title menu, save/load (localStorage)
- Character creator: name, class (Warrior / Mage / Rogue),
  customizable skin / hair / shirt / pants colors with live preview
- Multiple maps:
    - Overworld (forest, paths, river, fields)
    - Pixel Village (3 enterable houses)
    - Crypt of Shadows dungeon
    - Dark Spire dungeon (gated by a quest)
    - 3 cozy interiors (Healer, Smith, Granny)
- 5 enemy types with unique sprites: Slime, Cave Bat, Skeleton,
  Goblin, and the Dark Lord boss
- Turn-based combat: Attack / Magic / Defend / Flee, XP, levels,
  random damage variance, free-action "defend" reduces incoming damage
- 6 quests / missions with NPC givers, kill / collect / event goals,
  and rewards (XP, gold, items)
- Inventory, Healer NPC, treasure chests
- Day-cycle-style camera follow, smooth movement, walking animation

Controls
--------
- Move      WASD / Arrow keys
- Interact  E / Space (talk, read sign, open chest, enter door)
- Pause / Menu  Tab
- Combat:   Attack J · Magic K · Defend L · Flee F

Tip: walking onto an outdoor portal auto-enters it.  House doors
and dungeon entrances always require a press of E.

Running locally
---------------
Any static HTTP server works.  Examples:

    python3 -m http.server 8000
    # then open http://localhost:8000

Project layout
--------------
    index.html          — page + UI overlays
    css/style.css       — all styling
    js/sprites.js       — palettes + procedural pixel renderer
    js/maps.js          — overworld, village, dungeons, interiors
    js/input.js         — keyboard handling
    js/quests.js        — quest definitions & progress tracking
    js/combat.js        — turn-based combat
    js/ui.js            — title, character creator, dialog, HUD
    js/game.js          — main game loop, world & interactions

Saves are kept in `localStorage` under the key `pixelrealm_save`.
